                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Choose Wisely is a choice-driven adventure created and published by ID Card, built around the concept that every decision can dramatically reshape the story. Rather than following a single predetermined protagonist, the game places control over a diverse cast of nine playable characters whose lives become entangled after a mysterious and dangerous incident. Combining elements of adventure, RPG, strategy, and simulation, it focuses far more on narrative progression and player freedom than on traditional combat-heavy gameplay. Its greatest appeal lies in allowing players to influence events through meaningful choices, making each journey feel personal and unpredictable.\n\nThe story opens with an intriguing scenario as several strangers awaken in an unfamiliar location under mysterious circumstances. As they search for answers, they discover they have become unwilling participants in a deadly situation orchestrated by an unseen force. Suspicion grows with every encounter, and the game gradually reveals hidden motives, unexpected alliances, and dangerous secrets that encourage players to question every decision they make. The mystery unfolds at a steady pace, rewarding those who pay attention to dialogue and character interactions. Instead of relying solely on dramatic action sequences, the game creates tension through uncertainty, forcing players to carefully consider both immediate consequences and long-term outcomes.\n\nOne of the game's standout features is its extensive branching structure. Every major choice has the potential to alter relationships, determine who survives, unlock unique story events, or send the narrative toward an entirely different conclusion. With nine playable characters, nearly fifty possible party combinations, and more than fifty branching story routes, Choose Wisely offers remarkable replay value despite its relatively short playtime. A complete playthrough can be finished within a few hours, but experiencing the full scope of the game's content requires multiple runs, each revealing new dialogue, different alliances, and alternative endings that significantly change the overall narrative.\n\nWhile role-playing mechanics are present, they are designed to support the storytelling rather than overshadow it. Combat encounters are straightforward and accessible, giving each character distinct abilities without overwhelming players with complex systems. Those who prefer a stronger emphasis on narrative can also minimize the focus on battles, allowing the experience to become even more story-centric. This flexibility makes the game appealing to players who enjoy interactive fiction as much as those who appreciate light RPG mechanics. Character diversity also helps keep each playthrough fresh, as different party members contribute unique perspectives and abilities that influence both gameplay and dialogue.\n\nVisually, the game embraces a classic RPG-inspired presentation with detailed character artwork and environments that effectively communicate the unsettling atmosphere. Although the graphics are relatively modest compared to larger-budget productions, they complement the narrative well by emphasizing mood over technical spectacle. The soundtrack further enhances the experience with music that reinforces moments of mystery, danger, and emotional tension. Combined with solid writing and distinct personalities for each playable character, the audiovisual presentation succeeds in drawing players deeper into the unfolding drama.\n\nChoose Wisely succeeds because it fully commits to its central idea that choices should genuinely matter. Rather than presenting the illusion of player agency, it delivers meaningful branching paths that encourage experimentation and replayability. Its compelling mystery, varied cast, and numerous possible outcomes make every decision feel significant, while its approachable RPG systems ensure the focus remains on storytelling. Although players seeking deep tactical combat may find the gameplay mechanics somewhat simple, those who appreciate narrative adventures with multiple endings and lasting consequences will find plenty to enjoy. It is a memorable experience that demonstrates how effective player-driven storytelling can be when supported by thoughtful design and strong replay value.\n\nRating: 6/10",
